  "description": "PyCmaSampler for OptunaSharp — a native OptunaSharp BaseSampler that drives the real pycma (Nikolaus Hansen's `cma` package: cma.CMAEvolutionStrategy + cma.BoundTransform) library in-process via Python.NET (pythonnet). A faithful C# port of optuna_integration's PyCmaSampler glue (the sampler protocol + the parameter/cma-space transforms + the ask/tell generation replay) whose CMA-ES numerics are direct pycma calls, so it is byte-exact with pycma. Distinct from OptunaSharp's native CmaEsSampler, which ports the separate `cmaes` package — this mirrors Optuna's own optuna.integration.PyCmaSampler vs optuna.samplers.CmaEsSampler split. Does NOT require the Python optuna_integration package — install only `cma`. The .NET analog of using optuna_integration.PyCmaSampler, built on OptunaSharp.Interop.pythonnet. Part of the SciSharp STACK.",
  "iconFile": "optunasharp-icon.png",
